{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778898925,"nonce":"AK2kF/R3zywXQLnI3hlkMR7u8sQ=","title":"Session registry marks current process PID stale","message":"## Problem\n`readPidStartTime(process.pid)` recomputes `Date.now() - process.uptime()` every time it is called. Small millisecond drift between registration and liveness checking can make the same process appear to have a different start time, causing `SessionRegistry.getSessionByPid(process.pid)` to return no active session.\n\n## Context\nThis surfaced while verifying the phase 2 dist-file repair: `test/registry.test.ts -t \"getSessionByPid returns matching active session\"` fails consistently with `expected null to be truthy`. The failure is not caused by the generated dist files, but it blocks a clean suite.\n\n## Proposed Fix\nCache the current process start-time estimate once per module load and reuse it for `process.pid`, while leaving external PID lookup via `ps` unchanged.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}